  "_source": "AUTHORED, not fetched. Written in BPML (Barkpark.PortableDoc.Bpml, source beside this file as design-probe.bpml) and parsed to blocks \u2014 there is no published paper behind it, so fetch-fixtures.sh must never be pointed at this slug. It carries the shapes the six real papers do not: sections as `section` CONTAINERS (eyebrow + h2 heads INSIDE the container, which no top-level `> #paper-body > \u2026 > h2` leg reaches, so the section-head device does not size them); consecutive containers (whose trailing and leading `PdHr` stack into one doubled boundary); and a content-NARROW table (whose box centres on the evidence band while its ink pins to the band's left edge). All three are MEASURED in the report and none is asserted \u2014 each is an open finding with its own task, and a fixture that red-lined on them could not be committed.",
